# check: fail error[E21]: a nested '[...]' is a literal of the element its literal takes, and Array<I64>& is no type a literal makes
# E21: a nested row is made where the element is held by value (an Array<T>, a type with FromIter), never as a reference
fn main() {
    a := Array<Array<I64>&>[[1, 2], [3, 4]]
    assert a.Len() == 2
}
